    <div class="features-grid">
      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon-wrapper">⚙️</div>
        <h3 class="feature-title">256-Register VM</h3>
        <p class="feature-desc">
          Executes compact bytecode directly across fixed registers (r0..r255), eliminating recursive stack frames and object allocations during render loops.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon-wrapper">⚡</div>
        <h3 class="feature-title">Zero VDOM Diffing</h3>
        <p class="feature-desc">
          State changes trigger microtask updates that re-execute only the exact bytecode instructions bound to dirty variables. Updates patch DOM nodes directly in-place.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon-wrapper">📦</div>
        <h3 class="feature-title">AOT Bytecode Compiler</h3>
        <p class="feature-desc">
          Single File Components (.drift) compile at build time into an optimized binary-like bytecode stream and static constant pool, keeping runtime footprints tiny.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon-wrapper">🏝️</div>
        <h3 class="feature-title">Islands Architecture SSG</h3>
        <p class="feature-desc">
          Drift Static meta-framework delivers 0 kB JavaScript on static pages, hydrating interactive widgets selectively with client:load, client:visible, and client:idle.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon-wrapper">🔄</div>
        <h3 class="feature-title">Keyed LIS Reconciliation</h3>
        <p class="feature-desc">
          List rendering with &#64;for directive computes the Longest Increasing Subsequence to minimize physical DOM node movements, with fast-path attribute patching.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-card">
        <div class="feature-icon-wrapper">🌊</div>
        <h3 class="feature-title">Streaming SSR and Hydration</h3>
        <p class="feature-desc">
          DriftServerVM renders virtual server node trees to static HTML with comment delimiters (&lt;!--if--&gt;, &lt;!--for--&gt;), claiming DOM nodes efficiently on client hydration.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

